# fixedbugs, defect 569, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R2).
#
# Beside `run/fixedbugs-569-a-library-s-own-sign-conversion-is-not-the-program-s`:
# the header's own code is passed over, and the binding is not.
#
# SYMPTOM: `twice(x: u64)` against the header's `int twice(int)` was told
# as the header not compiling, at its own line, never as the declaration.
#
# FIX: a group's header is included inside a region of its own
# (`emit/header_region.hero`): `-Wall` and `-Wsign-conversion` are ignored
# there, a missing return and an uninitialised read stay errors, and after
# it every check of a binding is raised again (`emit/checks_raised.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-569-a-wrong-sign-through-a-library-s-header-is-the-binding-s.h"
    function twice(x: u32) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(twice(x: 21))
